<title>USA: Avery Dennison files $150 mln shelf debt.</title>
<headline>Avery Dennison files $150 mln shelf debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Avery Dennison Corp filed Tuesday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission for the offering of up to $150 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to reduce variate rate borrowings, reduce or retire other outstanding debt and for general corporate puposes.</p>
<p>The Pasadena, Calif.,-based maker of self-adhesive materials used for making labels and other office products did not name underwriters.</p>
</text>
